
# Movie API

## Description
A simple REST API built using Node.js and Express.js to manage movie details.

## Technologies Used
- Node.js
- Express.js
- JavaScript

## Installation

Install the required package:

```bash
npm init -y
npm install express
```

## Run the Server

```bash
node server.js
```

Server URL: `http://localhost:8080`

## API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| POST | `/api` | Add a movie |
| GET | `/api` | Get movie details |
| PUT | `/api/movies/:id` | Update a movie |
| DELETE | `/api/movies/:id` | Delete a movie |

## Example POST Request

URL: `http://localhost:8080/api`

Body (JSON):

```json
{
  "title": "Inception",
  "director": "Christopher Nolan",
  "genre": "SciFi",
  "rating": 8.8,
  "durationMinutes": 148,
  "nowShowing": false
}
```

## Testing
Use Postman or Thunder Client to test the API.

## Note
- Movie data is stored in memory.
- Data is lost when the server restarts.
- PUT and DELETE endpoints require code corrections to work properly.

